meta {
  name: Get Lab Adapter Lab Test Options
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/lab-adapters/lab-test-options?branchIds={{branchId}}&search=
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  branchIds: {{branchId}}
  search:
  ~page: 1
  ~limit: 20
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

script:post-response {
  const body = res.getBody();
  const rows = body && body.data && (body.data.data || body.data);
  if (Array.isArray(rows) && rows.length && rows[0].id) bru.setEnvVar("labAdapterLabTestOptionId", rows[0].id);
}

tests {
  test("200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });
}

docs {
  Options for the **Add / Edit Lab Adapter** form's manual **Lab Tests** picker.

  Every branch keeps its own copy of a test, but the picker lists each test
  **once**: copies of the same test (same **Test Name + Test Code**, compared
  case-insensitively and trimmed — the same rule the equipment auto-map uses)
  are folded into one option. Saving the adapter with that option links **every
  copy** at the adapter's branches (see Create / Update Lab Adapter), so the
  stored rows are still one per branch copy.

  The tests offered are the active, default-variant tests of each selected
  branch's default (Walk-in) list — the same row set the equipment auto-map
  draws from.

  **Query**
  - `branchIds` (required, 1–100) — the branches selected in the form, as a
    comma-separated list (`a,b`) or repeated (`branchIds=a&branchIds=b`); each a
    UUID v4. Taken from the query, not the JWT's active branch, because an
    adapter is tenant-level and a Business Admin has no active branch. Missing,
    empty or a non-UUID value → `400 VALIDATION_ERROR`. Every id is verified
    against the caller's tenant → `422 LAB_ADAPTER_BRANCH_NOT_FOUND` when one is
    not an active branch of it.
  - `search` (optional) — case-insensitive match on the test name.
  - `page` / `limit` (optional, `limit` ≤ 100) — omit `page` for the full array
    in `data`; supply it for a page in `data` plus `meta { total, page, limit,
    totalPages }` (the standard envelope). The
    frontend's shared `optionFetcher` always supplies both. Grouping happens
    before paging, so `total` counts tests, not branch copies.

  **Response row**
  ```json
  {
    "id": "5f0c…",
    "name": "Complete Blood Count (CBC)",
    "branchId": "a3eca72a-…",
    "branchIds": ["a3eca72a-…", "65a6800d-…"],
    "hint": "All selected branches"
  }
  ```
  - `id` — one copy's id: the copy at the first selected branch that has the test
    (any copy works; saving expands the pick to all copies).
  - `name` — `Test Name (CODE)`; the code part is omitted when the test has none.
    The label no longer carries a branch name.
  - `branchId` — the branch of the copy that `id` belongs to.
  - `branchIds` — every selected branch that has a copy of the test.
  - `hint` — only when two or more branches are selected: `All selected
    branches` when every selected branch has the test, otherwise the names of the
    branches that do. Absent for a single branch.

  Rows are ordered by test name.

  **Used by:** the Lab Adapter form's Lab Tests picker (`PaginatedSelect`, shown
  once per test with the `hint` beside it).
}
